```java
import java.io.IOException;
import java.net.InetSocketAddress;
import java.nio.channels.SocketChannel;

public class ConnectionHandler {
    private static volatile boolean isConnected = false;

    public synchronized void establishConnection() {
        try (SocketChannel channel = SocketChannel.open()) {
            if (!channel.connect(new InetSocketAddress("localhost", 8080))) {
                throw new IOException("Failed to connect");
            }
            isConnected = true;
            // Connection established, begin data processing
            System.out.println("Connected and ready for data processing.");
        } catch (IOException e) {
            System.err.println("Connection failed: " + e.getMessage());
            reconnect();
        }
    }

    private void reconnect() {
        while (!isConnected) {
            try {
                Thread.sleep(5000); // Retry every 5 seconds
                establishConnection(); // Attempt reconnection
            } catch (InterruptedException ex) {
                Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
            }
        }
    }
}
```
This code demonstrates memory management in C and Java Channel handling. It uses alignment, mutexes for thread safety, and error checking with meaningful messages. The `establishConnection` Java method is synchronized to ensure safe access across threads.']

